                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0ec6d489-0c1a-3076-b65e-6101f6e19c10",
                        "entry_id": "66211598-ea6c-3ca6-8ace-1d026f836b95",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A flavonol found in many fruits, vegetables, leaves and grains."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4a5bcac9-e5f7-41c5-8bc1-77425ace9e89",
                                "sense_id": "0ec6d489-0c1a-3076-b65e-6101f6e19c10",
                                "text": "Quercetin has gained the attention of the supplement industry, and is now widely promoted as a natural anti-inflammatory and antioxidant magic bullet."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e686f541-2f4f-4a61-967c-fc3cb156d1dd",
                                "sense_id": "0ec6d489-0c1a-3076-b65e-6101f6e19c10",
                                "text": "The one daily supplement that often reduces allergic symptoms across the board is the phytonutrient quercetin, a chemical compound known as a bioflavonoid and found in plants."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d102e2c-6ff1-4c8f-abf4-8b7c2284ac11",
                                "sense_id": "0ec6d489-0c1a-3076-b65e-6101f6e19c10",
                                "text": "In plasma, quercetin mostly exists as glucuronated, sulfated, and/or methylated quercetin conjugates."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ac98e78f-31b8-47ec-a034-2607b314f4a0",
                                "sense_id": "0ec6d489-0c1a-3076-b65e-6101f6e19c10",
                                "text": "One study, for example, found that eating a diet rich in quercetin, found in green tea, broccoli and red wine, might help protect against lung cancer, especially in heavy smokers."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
